{
  "_source": "lingxi-telemetry::tengu::ALL_EVENT_NAMES (lingxi-core/crates/telemetry/src/tengu/mod.rs) — M3-06 schema lock against claude-code @ 6a25909 src/services/statsig.ts::logStatsigEvent wire shape.",
  "_note": "tengu_* event names in registration order: api (25) -> agent (30) -> session (20) -> tool (134) -> cost (10) -> oauth (8) -> memory (12) -> settings (3). The tool block is 40 (M3-06 baseline) MINUS 6 (grep/glob: claude-code v2.1.183 emits NO tengu_tool_grep_* / tengu_tool_glob_* telemetry, so the port emits none either) + 9 (M4-02 powershell/repl/sleep) + 3 (M4-03 web_search) + 15 (M4-04 workflow: todo_write/{enter,exit}_plan_mode/{enter,exit}_worktree) + 24 (M4-05 agent/task: agent/task_{create,get,list,update,stop,output}/send_message) + 6 (M4-06 team: team_{create,delete}) + 13 (M4-07 mcp/lsp: mcp_started + mcp_auth/list_mcp_resources/read_mcp_resource/lsp × started/completed/failed; MCP_COMPLETED + MCP_FAILED were already in the M3-06 baseline). Order is append-only per spec §7 line 787-789; adding a name MUST extend the list and bump the count. Removing a name is a v0.5+ breaking change. Field-set changes to existing events use sibling tengu_<name>_v2 names with a 2-minor deprecation cycle. M5-13: orchestrator block grows 15 -> 17 (+2 tengu_repl_session_started/ended). M5-14: + lingxi_core_v0_6_0_released release marker (+1 -> 315). M6-01: tui block (+4 tengu_tui_session_started/ended/first_render/resize -> 319). M6-03: tui block +2 (streaming_render_started/ended -> 321). M6-05: tui block +2 (permission_dialog_shown/resolved -> 323). M6-09: + lingxi_core_v0_7_0_released release marker (+1 -> 324) + tui block +2 (scroll_started/ended -> 326); tengu_tui_key_pressed deferred to M7. M7-01..M7-15: +0 (every TUI event candidate deferred to the M7-16 audit). M7-16: + lingxi_core_v0_8_0_released release marker (+1) + tui block +3 (screen_opened/screen_closed/search_opened, real emit sites; command_palette_opened/vim_mode_entered/key_pressed deferred to M8). Total (after the -6 grep/glob removal): 324. CronDelete/CronList: +6 (2 tools × 3 lifecycle stages) -> 330. FileReadTool analytics: +4 appended at the GLOBAL TAIL (tengu_file_read_dedup, tengu_session_file_read, tengu_file_read_limits_override, tengu_file_read_reread [#13]) — NOT tengu_tool_* events, so kept after the tui block to preserve per-block prefix slices -> 334. Config migrations: +9 appended as their own tail block (tengu_migrate_autoupdates_to_settings/_error, tengu_migrate_bypass_permissions_accepted, tengu_migrate_mcp_approval_fields_success/_error, tengu_reset_pro_to_opus_default, tengu_legacy_opus_migration, tengu_sonnet45_to_46_migration, tengu_opus_to_opus1m_migration; runMigrations port, order matches main.tsx:328-336) -> 343. Permission flow: +1 bypass dialog (tengu_bypass_permissions_mode_dialog_accept, BypassPermissionsModeDialog.tsx accept branch) appended as its own tail block after the config-migration block -> 344. Coordinator swarm: +3 appended as their own global-tail block after the permission block (tengu_team_created, tengu_team_deleted, tengu_coordinator_mode_switched; claude-code coordinator emit sites TeamCreateTool.ts:214 / TeamDeleteTool.ts:111 / coordinatorMode.ts:71) -> 347. 2.1.198 M2 AWS auth-refresh trust gate: +2 appended as their own global-tail block after the coordinator block (tengu_awsAuthRefresh_missing_trust, tengu_awsCredentialExport_missing_trust; binary ZBd / t2d emit `G(name,{})` when a project/local-sourced command is refused before workspace trust) -> 343. Worktree feature (2.1.206): +4 tengu_worktree_* events INSIDE the tool block (not a tail block) — tengu_worktree_created/tengu_worktree_entered_existing inserted immediately after tengu_tool_enter_worktree_failed, and tengu_worktree_kept/tengu_worktree_removed inserted immediately after tengu_tool_exit_worktree_failed, matching telemetry/src/tengu/tool.rs::NAMES order -> 347. 2.1.251 byte-alignment B8 (telemetry-modules): +2 tengu_mcp_* analytics events appended as their own global-tail block after the AWS auth-refresh block (tengu_mcp_server_config_invalid, tengu_mcp_tools_listed — the only two confirmed real tengu_mcp_* ANALYTICS events at the oracle; everything else with that prefix is a Statsig feature-flag name) -> 349. +14 tengu_plugin_* events appended as their own global-tail block after the MCP block (tengu_plugin_enabled_for_session and 13 siblings; the port had no plugin telemetry module before this) -> 363. 2.1.251 §20a/§20b wiring: +1 tengu_mcp_degraded appended to the MCP block (traced to yn's per-server tool-schema-classification tail and qr's process-global validator-unavailable fallback; this is where normalizedCount/keptCount actually live, NOT on tengu_mcp_tools_listed) -> 364.",
